    {
      "title": "UniFi Access Point | Releases | Ubiquiti Community",
      "feedUrl": "https://community.ui.com/rss/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-Switch/9fc3b2fa-9e73-449a-924f-470e79884470",
      "siteUrl": "https://community.ui.com",
      "articles": [
        {
          "id": "07f28441-5018-4c5e-82ed-f2a7e20481e2",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Improvements\n\nImproved network self-healing: APs now consistently revert to stable wired connections, automatically clearing unintended wireless paths after topology changes.\n\nAdditional information\nUpdate your devices by changing the Device Firmware Release Channel in the UniFi Network application to Release Candidate.\n\nIf you wish to go back to the Official release after the upgrade, change the release channel back to Official.\n\nIf you encounter any issues with this release, please provide us with some details on your setup and include the below information:\n\nAP model(s)\nPrevious AP release version\nUniFi Network application version",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-for-U7-LR-8-0-64/07f28441-5018-4c5e-82ed-f2a7e20481e2",
          "publishedOn": "2026-02-03T12:41:42.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point for U7-LR 8.0.64",
          "imageUrl": null
        },
        {
          "id": "e57d76ae-1bbd-4e95-818f-185afc0961f2",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Overview\nThis release is only for these models:\n\nU6-LR/U6-Lite/U6+\nUAP-nanoHD/FlexHD/BeaconHD/IW-HD\n\nImprovements\n\nImproved network self-healing: APs now consistently revert to stable wired connections, automatically clearing unintended wireless paths after topology changes.\n\nAdditional information\nUpdate your devices by changing the Device Firmware Release Channel in the UniFi Network application to Release Candidate.\n\nIf you wish to go back to the Official release after the upgrade, change the release channel back to Official.\n\n----\nIf you encounter any issues with this release, please provide us with some details on your setup and include the below information:\n\nAP model(s)\nPrevious AP release version\nUniFi Network application version",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-for-U6-LR-U6-Lite-U6-and-more-6-7-41/e57d76ae-1bbd-4e95-818f-185afc0961f2",
          "publishedOn": "2026-02-03T12:40:03.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point for U6-LR, U6-Lite, U6+ & more 6.7.41",
          "imageUrl": null
        },
        {
          "id": "5c86022f-7c88-4d2b-ac5b-753b95985c5a",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Overview\nThis release applies for these models:\n\nUAP-AC-Lite/LR/Pro/M/M-PRO/IW/UK-Ultra\nUAP-HD/SHD/XG/BaseStationXG\nU6-Pro/Mesh/IW/Extender/Enterprise/Enterprise-IW\n\nImprovements\n\nImproved network self-healing: APs now consistently revert to stable wired connections, automatically clearing unintended wireless paths after topology changes.\n\nAdditional information\nUpdate your devices by changing the Device Firmware Release Channel in the UniFi Network application to Release Candidate.\n\nIf you wish to go back to the Official release after the upgrade, change the release channel back to Official.\n\n----\nIf you encounter any issues with this release, please provide us with some details on your setup and include the below information:\n\nAP model(s)\nPrevious AP release version\nUniFi Network application version",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-for-U6-Pro-U6-Enterprise-U6-Mesh-and-more-6-8-2/5c86022f-7c88-4d2b-ac5b-753b95985c5a",
          "publishedOn": "2026-02-03T12:39:13.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point for U6-Pro, U6-Enterprise, U6-Mesh & more 6.8.2",
          "imageUrl": null
        },
        {
          "id": "a2e0cac9-f769-48ff-828b-7a6f76c13c53",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Overview\nThis release is promoted to Official/Stable release channel for these models:\n\n\nU7-Pro - January 22, 2026\nU7-Pro-Max, U7-Pro-Wall, U7-Pro-XG, U7-Pro-XGS, U7-Pro-XG-Wall, U7-Pro-Outdoor - January 26, 2026\nU7-Lite, U7-Outdoor, U7-In-Wall, E7, E7-Campus, E7-Audience - January 26, 2026\n\nImprovements\n\nImproved network self-healing: APs now consistently revert to stable wired connections, automatically clearing unintended wireless paths after topology changes.\n\nAdditional information\nINFO: U7-LR model support will be added in upcoming releases.\n----\nUpdate your devices by changing the Device Firmware Release Channel in the UniFi Network application to Release Candidate.\n\nIf you wish to go back to the Official release after the upgrade, change the release channel back to Official.\n\nIf you encounter any issues with this release, please provide us with some details on your setup and include the below information:\n\nAP model(s)\nPrevious AP release version\nUniFi Network application version\nUniFi Console Support File (as private attachment)",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-all-U7-and-E7-models-8-4-6/a2e0cac9-f769-48ff-828b-7a6f76c13c53",
          "publishedOn": "2026-01-14T20:54:58.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point (all U7 and E7 models) 8.4.6",
          "imageUrl": null
        }
      ]
    },
